lesson: 133
title: So many times more, so many times fewer
level: primary-2
stars: 0
explain: «3 times as many» (or «3 times more») means the smaller number taken 3 times: 3 times as many as 5 is 5 × 3 = 15.
explain: «Ann has 3 times fewer than Ben» says the same thing from the other side: Ben has 3 times as many as Ann.
explain: So if Ann has 5 and that is 3 times fewer than Ben has, Ben has 5 × 3 = 15.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing x=2..12 k=2..6
need: x * k <= 60
answer: x * k
exercise: {a} has {x} {t}. {b} has {k} times as many {t} as {a}. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: {a} has {x} {t}, and {b} has {k} times more. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: {a} has {x} {t}. That is {k} times fewer than {b} has. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: {a} has {k} times fewer {t} than {b}. {a} has {x}. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: {b} collected {k} times as many {t} as {a}. {a} collected {x}. How many {t} did {b} collect?
exercise: The number of {t} {a} has is {k} times smaller than the number {b} has. {a} has {x} {t}. How many does {b} have?
test: {b}'s {t} are {k} times as many as {a}'s {x}. How many {t} has {b} got?
test: If {x} {t} is what {a} has and {b} has {k} times that number, how many {t} does {b} have?
test: {a} has only {x} {t}, {k} times fewer than {b}. Find how many {t} {b} has.
test: {a}'s pile of {x} {t} is {k} times smaller than {b}'s pile. How many {t} are in {b}'s pile?
exercise: How many {t} does {b} have, if {a} has {x} {t} and {b} has {k} times as many?
exercise: {a}: {x} {t}. {b}: {k} times as many. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: In Texas, {a} picked {x} {t}, and {b} picked {k} times more than that. How many {t} did {b} pick?
exercise: {a} has {x.words} {t}. {b} has {k.words} times as many {t}. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: {a} has {k} times fewer {t} than {b}. If {a} has {x} {t}, how many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: {b} has {k} times the number of {t} that {a} has. {a} has {x}. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: At a summer camp in Ontario, {a} found {x} {t}. That is {k} times less than {b} found. How many {t} did {b} find?
exercise: {a} owns {x} {t}, and {b} owns {k} times as many. Find the number of {t} {b} owns.
test: {b}, who lives in Sydney, has {k} times the {x} {t} that {a} has. What is {b}'s number of {t}?
test: {x} {t} belong to {a}. {b}'s collection is {k} times bigger. How big is {b}'s collection?
test: In Galway, {a} has {k} times fewer {t} than {b}; {a} has {x}. How many {t} has {b} got?
test: Take {a}'s {x} {t} {k} times, and you get {b}'s {t}. How many {t} does {b} have?
test: {a}'s {x.words} {t} are {k.words} times fewer than {b}'s. Count {b}'s {t}.
test: {b} in Christchurch has {k} times as many {t} as {a}, who has {x}. How many does {b} have?
exercise: {a} got {x} {t}, {b} got {k} times as many. how many {b} got
exercise: {a}'s got {x+1} {t} — no wait, {x}. {b} has {k} times more. how many has {b}
exercise: {b} says if {a} has {x} {t} and {b} got {k} times as many, thats {x*k+x}. nah. how many {b} got really
exercise: {a} has {x} {t} ({a.his} mum paid 5 dollars for em), {b} has {k} times as many. how many {t} {b} got
test: {b} has {k} times what {a} has, {a} has {x} {t}. {b}'s total?
test: {a}: {x} {t}. thats {k} times less than {b}. how many {b} got
test: {a} has {x} {t}, {b} has {k+1} times — no wait, {k} times as many. how many {t} for {b}
exam: It is given that {a} holds {x} {t} and that the holding of {b} is {k} times as great. Determine the number of {t} held by {b}.
exam: Whereas the {x} {t} held by {a} constitute {k} times fewer than those held by {b}, ascertain the holding of {b}.
exam: The holding of {b} is a {k}-fold multiple of the holding of {a}, the latter being {x} {t}. State the number of {t} held by {b}.
exam: Compute the quantity which is {k} times the magnitude of {x}.
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {a} {x} stamps, and he left {b} {k} times as many. How many stamps did {b} get?
exercise: {a} was economical with the truth: {a.he} said {a.he} ate {x} cookies. Actually {a.he} ate {k} times as many. How many cookies did {a.he} really eat?
test: {b} says {b.he} "only had a couple", what a load of crap. {b.he} had {k} times as many as me and i had {x} {t}. how many did {b.he} have
